WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:07.360
You've made it to the end of this course on translucent materials and visual effects.

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.910
Congratulations, and thank you for being part of this class.

3
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.589
Let's take a moment to review what we've learned in these past lessons.

4
00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:19.989
First of all, we explored the world of translucent materials,

5
00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:22.269
familiarizing with the Fresnel and

6
00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:26.750
refraction indexes to achieve the looks and effects we wanted.

7
00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:32.750
We also learned about advanced nodes like the bump offset and the spiral blur.

8
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.270
Further on, we looked into the two-sided foliage shading model and

9
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.909
set up a material with a cute little wind effect on its lips.

10
00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:45.189
But you could really use the simple grasswind material function for

11
00:00:45.189 --> 00:00:49.909
other things like blankets, flags, whatever you want.

12
00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:54.350
Lastly, we developed a dissolve effect using a material function,

13
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.630
reviewing again how to deal with function inputs in that specific case and

14
00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.380
get that set up.

15
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.500
Thank you again for sticking around.

16
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.930
I really hope you've enjoyed this course and learned a few tricks from it.

17
00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.250
You're welcome to take a glimpse at the other courses on our platform

18
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.409
to further expand your understanding of the engine.

19
00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.890
Have lots of fun tinkering with materials in Unreal, and I'll see you soon.

20
00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.390
Bye.
